The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=16$) is the interval between $x=15$ and $x=17$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
f'(16)&\approx\dfrac{f(17)-f(15)}{17-15}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-68-(-63)}{2}
\\\\
&=-2.5
\end{align}$
